Let us hope that David is right, and that we can convince our many scientific
authors that they _are not_ master typographers, that they better spend their
time on improving the content of a paper, rather than its presentation.
But if the latter is important, then there should, of course, be tools for
doing the job. Yet, that can be left to the package designer, who can choose
the fonts that are needed.

